# Overrides .env for `npm run dev` only (Vite loads `.env.[mode]` on top of
# `.env`, and `vite`/`vite dev` run in "development" mode by default --
# https://vite.dev/guide/env-and-mode). Local dev always serves the bundle
# you just built (`fvm flutter build web -t lib/main_web.dart
# --no-web-resources-cdn`, or `scripts/run_example_web.sh`) from the
# `build_web` symlink -- never the CDN, which can silently drift out of
# sync with your working tree's actual interface contract (see the
# marketTiming/marketTimings mismatch this was written to prevent: the CDN
# bundle predated a host-contract change, and pointing dev at it produced a
# confusing runtime failure that had nothing to do with the code being
# worked on). `npm run build` is unaffected -- it still defaults to the CDN
# via `.env`, matching what a real deployed host would load.
VITE_SDK_ASSET_BASE=/build_web/
